Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
even though total war warhammer 3  features some of the more niche factions  in games workshop's old world it makes  it all the more impressive that creative  assembly have managed to make the third  entry into this trilogy the largest and  most dynamic as game sports resident  warhammer nerd i got to play a few hours  with a preview build of total war  warhammer 3. specifically the campaigns  of grand cafe and the newly announced  pick and mix of demons chaos undivided  and while the other races of  kisslevite's demons and ogres were  unplayable they certainly made their  presence known on the battlefield with  the addition of chaos undivided that  brings the number of playable races at  launch up to eight those being nurgle  slaanesh zinch korn chaos undivided  kislev the ogre kingdoms and grand  cathay no matter the choice however it  appears that each faction's story will  see them heading to the realms of chaos  themselves creative assembly have stated  that this game's map is twice the size  as the previous entry and the home of  each chaos god will certainly help make  up a portion of that as the story  progresses rifts will open up in the  world allowing you to enter a realm of  your choosing each with its own unique  challenges and gameplay nurgle is full  of disease and players must find  resistances and cures before they lose  armies to attrition corn will only allow  you to delve deeper into his domain  after spilling enough blood zinc's realm  is made of riddles and you must choose  the correct teleporter runes to delve  deeper into the realm and slaanesh is  based around challenging descents  through circles of depravity each god  will also tempt you with rewards of  items resistances currency alliances  with chaotic forces and more however the  trade-off is a permanent negative trait  tied to your character so it'll be up to  you to choose whether or not these boons  are worth the price you pay but it is  only at the center of these realms that  you will face the new challenging final  survival battles of the particular chaos  god you are of course competing with  every other faction too so it's more  than likely that you'll encounter armies  from across the campaign here in the  realms of chaos be they friend or foe  cathay was the first faction i chose to  play as as i was intrigued to see how  creative assembly could build a faction  that previously only existed as snippets  of lore within the warhammer fantasy  books these dragon defenders of the  great bastion share their starting point  with a great wall separating themselves  from a never-ending tide of chaos  invasion this defensive element to their  start and their law is mirrored in the  units that they can field but with it  comes one key element that is unique to  their forces harmony and balance is a  core feature to grand cathay and nearly  every facet of their economy buildings  research and army reflect either an  element of yin or yang in the world map  keeping harmony will grant buffs to  things like growth and public order  whereas being too heavily weighted in  either direction will cause  destabilization this essence of harmony  can also affect your units in battle  with each also having an element to yin  or yank ensuring units of opposite  alignment are close together during  battles will boost their stats and make  them all the more capable in combat this  extra level of strategy is minor but  it's a great feeling when you combine  units to become a balanced and  harmonious force that is more than the  sum of their parts grand cathay also has  a few features that play into unique  mechanics as well as their lore and map  location their wushing compass allows  them to alter the winds of magic across  their lands allowing you to set up buffs  and bonuses for future battles or make  life that little bit harder for the  enemies beyond your walls and the  location of the ivory road means that  cathay and forces can send trade  caravans westward to the old world and  the further you send them the better the  profit but beware as both dilemmas and  rewards exist on these trails these  caravans work much like generals or be  it ones that you won't control directly  in the world map instead you'll set them  off on their journey and they'll  periodically check in on you if anything  comes up during their travels it could  be anything from an empire captain  looking for work to ogres looking to you  as their next meal triggering a battle  and giving you the option to command  directly these events are great as they  allow you to feel like you have more  control over the fate of your caravans  and engaging with them often grants you  a little extra reward beyond the payday  of goods delivered  [Music]  now we were only made aware of the chaos  undivided faction at the start of our  hands-on with the game and while i'm  usually a stalwart follower of the  plague father i was very excited for the  ability to control an army of demons  from every god under the banner of a  single demon prince the main drive for  this faction is glory every time you win  a battle or take a settlement you have  the ability to dedicate this victory or  milestone to a chaos god and doing so  will grant you specific boons units and  even body parts the deeper your  dedication the bigger the rewards you  can opt in to diversify your favors and  as such get a little something from  every god to keep your arsenal and  roster diverse or you can choose to hone  in on a specific god and play style and  rush towards their more juicy rewards  and of course as you are indeed playing  as a demon prince these rewards can also  manifest physically nurgle could bless  you with wings corn a fiery armored  chest zinch the head of an avian beast  and slaanesh a tooth laden tail all of  these change the benefits your demon  prince brings to your game with many of  them offering unique abilities and  spells different fighting styles or just  beefing up the unit's health and armor  naturally you can also change these as  you see fit and on the fly meaning that  you can swap out the bits and pieces of  your own mortal form at will experiment  with builds and combinations from  different gods or fully devote your  flesh prison to the entity of your  choosing seeing the swathe of garish  colours in hellish forms taking the  field of battle after i'd ingratiated  myself with a selection of the warhammer  gods was equal parts magnificent and  hilarious but did also drive home that  emphasis of player choice  additional options for players seem to  have been a core goal throughout the  development of creative assembly's third  entry into the world of warhammer many  of the improvements and changes that the  team have made having quality of life  improvements as well as new or tweaked  features enhanced diplomacy opens up  better war coordination as well as the  option to pay for outposts to be built  in friendly allied territories which  will allow you to recruit a unit or two  from their roster battles have also had  some big changes in particular siege and  settlement battles for the unwarded  variety many of them are now able to be  assaulted from every angle these 360  degree balances of attack and defense  open up new strategic opportunities and  avenues of attack when it comes to the  walled in cities however changes to  sieges mean that there are more options  for defenders beyond garrison their  walls should the fight take to the  streets the defender has the option to  use total war warhammer 3's new supply  system letting generals throw up  defending towers or barricades to either  force fights into specific kill zones or  ensure the attacking force has to  dedicate resources into taking them down  previously siege battles would feel  pretty stale with the only option  seeming to be defend the wall or abandon  them entirely but now there are many  more options available to the defenders  this has had to be balanced for the  attacker however as attackers face enemy  units breach walls or take objectives  they will earn momentum giving them  buffs to their units to help counteract  any traps towers or barricades in the  short time i got to play i felt both  these elements working in tandem made  siege battles a much more strategic and  engaging affair there would be times  where i'd willingly give up a wall or  corner of my city because i knew i'd  built up enough supplies to make an even  stronger backline with troops already  awaiting me and as the attacker i felt a  drive to continue pushes and pincer  attacks knowing that my units were much  more stalwart driven on by the morale  boosts of each little victory through  breaches and objectives now we can hope  that these changes will be retroactively  applied to the previous games or at  least to their larger combined campaign  map but as of yet when we are going to  see that arrive in warhammer 3 has not  been confirmed although when i did speak  to some members of the team they did say  that post launch support will be similar  to what we've come to expect of this  franchise and that sometime down the  line a grand campaign and a suite of dlc  will be coming so something to be extra  excited about even beyond the launch of  total war warhammer 3 on the 17th of  february now i do have a gameplay video  ready for you right now showing off a  bit of my time with chaos undivided but  other than that i think that's all i've  got for you if you have more questions  you can feel free to throw them down  below or tweet me at regular dave and i  will do my best to answer them otherwise  i hope you enjoyed this little preview  of total war warhammer 3 make sure you  subscribe and i'll see you next time  [Music]  so  [Music]  you

